# Copy to backup.env (git-ignored), then ./dev k8s seal. Where the backup sidecar sends backups
# (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md → Backups): the restic REST server on the owner's big server, append-only.
#   RESTIC_REPOSITORY  rest:https://<user>:<password>@<big server>:8000/<user>/
#                      (the user and password are this cluster's line in the REST server's .htpasswd)
#   RESTIC_PASSWORD    encrypts every backup. Lose it and the backups can't be read: keep a copy
#                      off the machines too. Make it with: openssl rand -hex 32
#   RESTIC_CACERT_PEM  the CA that signed the REST server's certificate (the infra repo's CA), as one
#                      line: awk 'NF {printf "%s\\n", $0}' ca.crt. Leave it out for a publicly trusted one.
RESTIC_REPOSITORY=rest:https://avian:change-me@backup.lan:8000/avian/
RESTIC_PASSWORD=change-me
